## Exact implementation boundary

`GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor` now uses the concrete sealed `ControlledBenchmarkLeaseManager` (shared process-wide static generation even across instances) and `GenericGuardianControlledBenchmarkIntervalCapture` around BOTH actual typed capture calls. An active or changing Track0 benchmark during initial capture denies the mutation; a generation transition after before evidence but before mutation denies the mutation. After transaction start, a transition during mutation, during the second capture, during evidence collection or evaluator causes exact Track2 restore, Inconclusive, no retained lease/KEEP. The FIRST snapshot before capture is compared against the LAST authority snapshot around the entire cycle, detecting acquire+release even when both observations show Idle. Source-supplied `ControlledBenchmarkActive=false` does not override this gate. Test-only fake evidence deliberately reports false during injected actual lease transitions.

Existing action→capability authorization, real LiveSafe descriptor check, exact target/epoch/frame/timestamp comparison, typed evaluator and kept lease rollback remain intact; no Track0 gate authority modification. `ControlledBenchmarkLeaseManager` is optional as a constructor argument only for sharing an explicit manager; if omitted, executor creates an actual concrete manager reading the SAME global static gate. Callers cannot inject a fake probe as benchmark authority.

